---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '~/components/common/JsonLd.astro';
import { SITE } from 'astrowind:config';

const metadata = {
  title: `EVA Foam Technology — SUP Deck Pad Materials and Construction | ${SITE.name}`,
  description:
    'Technical deep dive into EVA foam used for SUP deck traction pads: material properties, die-cutting, laser engraving, multi-color block piecing, and adhesion methods.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'EVA Foam Technology for SUP Deck Pads',
  description: metadata.description,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name },
  datePublished: '2026-07-27',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <JsonLd data={jsonLd} />
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-sky-600">{SITE.name}</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><a
        href="/research"
        class="hover:text-sky-600">Research</a
      ><span class="mx-2">/</span><span class="text-gray-900">EVA Foam Technology</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="mb-4">
      <span
        class="inline-block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-600 bg-sky-50 px-3 py-1 rounded-full"
        >Materials</span
      ><span class="ml-3 text-sm text-gray-400">7 min read</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">EVA Foam Technology for SUP Deck Pads</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      The traction pad on an inflatable SUP is more than a comfort feature — it is a critical structural and aesthetic
      component. This guide explores EVA foam materials, construction methods, and quality indicators.
    </p>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-gray-900 prose-p:text-gray-600">
      <h2>What Is EVA Foam?</h2>
      <p>
        Ethylene-vinyl acetate (EVA) is a closed-cell foam copolymer widely used in SUP deck pads. Closed-cell structure
        means water cannot penetrate the foam, preventing waterlogging and bacterial growth. EVA provides excellent
        shock absorption, UV resistance, and durability. Typical density for SUP pads is 80-120 kg/m³ — dense enough for
        abrasion resistance but soft enough for barefoot comfort.
      </p>
      <h2>Dual-Layer EVA Construction</h2>
      <p>
        Premium SUP pads use dual-layer composite EVA with a softer top layer (for grip and comfort) bonded to a denser
        bottom layer (for structural integrity). The two layers are heat-laminated together before cutting. Total pad
        thickness ranges from 4mm to 8mm. Thicker pads offer more comfort but add weight and may reduce board rigidity
        feel.
      </p>
      <h2>Color-Block Piecing</h2>
      <p>
        Multi-color block piecing involves die-cutting shapes from different colored EVA sheets and puzzle-assembling
        them into a seamless pad. The die-cut edges are precisely matched so the assembled pattern has no gaps or
        overlaps. This technique creates permanent color — the colors are inherent to the EVA material, not printed on
        the surface. Afarer uses CNC die-cutting for sub-millimeter precision in color-block patterns.
      </p>
      <h2>Laser Engraving</h2>
      <p>
        Laser engraving uses a CO₂ laser to etch away the top colored layer of a dual-layer EVA pad, revealing the
        contrasting bottom layer. The result is a permanent, 3D-textured pattern that will never wear off. Laser
        parameters (power, speed, frequency) must be precisely controlled to achieve the correct engraving depth without
        burning through both layers. Afarer's Flowing Lotus series uses this technology for intricate lotus and koi
        patterns.
      </p>
      <h2>Mechanical Heat Embossing</h2>
      <p>
        Heat embossing uses a heated metal roller or stamp to press patterns into the EVA surface under controlled
        pressure and temperature. The compressed areas become denser and slightly recessed, creating a permanent 3D
        texture. Unlike laser engraving, embossing does not remove material — it compresses it. This technique is used
        for wave patterns and geometric textures on Afarer's Ocean Pulse and Leviathan Wake series.
      </p>
      <h2>Adhesion Methods</h2>
      <p>
        EVA pads are bonded to the PVC hull using either contact adhesive or heat-activated adhesive film. Contact
        adhesive is sprayed on both surfaces and allowed to become tacky before pressing together. Heat-activated film
        is placed between the pad and PVC, then heat-pressed to activate the bond. Heat bonding provides more consistent
        adhesion and eliminates solvent fumes. Afarer uses industrial-grade heat bonding for all production boards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
